00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.220
First appearance in Fantastic Four number 48 alongside Galactus.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.300
So that's pretty big deal. They came as a pair and silver surfer usually is the herald of Galactus.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:48.160
Although as we mentioned in our Punisher episode, sometimes whoever the herald of Galactus, sometimes it could be the Punisher.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.180
It could just be whoever.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:50.460
So is he cool?

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.540
Because the Punisher is. Like he's a nice boy?

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:53.720
No, no, no.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:05:00.640
So he's like kind of, you know, to Earth's problems, he could be like, oh my God, this guy's a villain.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:03.860
But to the cosmos, he's like a hero.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:10.200
You know, it's just that like Earth and the universe don't exactly have aligned goals, if that makes sense.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.280
Wow, it seems pretty, pretty messed up.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:26.680
Right. So think about the silver surfer as somebody who like for a very long time when introduced was seen as a villain because of their allegiance or rather, you know, enslavement to Galactus.

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.060
But he eats obviously.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.040
Yeah. Galactus eats the entire planet at once.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:40.140
Yeah. But the silver surfer eventually became like such a popular character that they were like, well, you know, it'd be a great idea.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.660
Give this guy his own comic book.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:47.060
And so silver surfer number one came out and they were like, well, you can't have a comic book like that if the guy's going to be a villain.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:54.960
So they started writing like more like, you know, morally gray stories for the silver surfer where he's not exactly.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.900
Morally silver, maybe. Yeah. Morally silver.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.080
And so that happens.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.040
That happens pretty early on.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:05.420
So if Fantastic Four number 48 was in 66 by 68, he's got his own line.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:15.700
And then in the 80s and 90s, he becomes a huge part of like the grander Marvel Galactic Universe stuff with like the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.840
Like he played a huge part of that, even though he didn't play it in the movies, obviously.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:28.120
He's the only person who's able to like with the assistance of Adam Warlock, like stop Thanos from wielding the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:38.660
So like the other Marvel superheroes are just kind of like distraction fodder for these more epic superheroes on the cosmic scale like the silver surfer.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:40.200
So the silver surfer is kind of a big deal.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.280
And sorry, we can get to the game in a second.

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:50.540
But like aside from surfing, which I'm sure he's very good at, what else can he do?

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.000
In terms of what?

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.000
Like super? How does he fight?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.720
Yeah. With his fists.

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.160
Okay. Is it super strong or is he just?

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.660
He's just got a cool surfboard and he happens to be made of metal.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.940
No, I don't think he's doing like surf tricks on Spider-Man.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.900
I don't think that's how he's handling.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:14.060
Yeah. But that's the problem though.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.640
It was like silver surfer has like cosmic powers.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.240
So like he, you know, he's like one of those like superheroes.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:21.640
He's like the ability to manipulate energy, right?

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:32.420
Like things that are just like stupid on the scale of like when we're talking about guys who fight rhinoceroses, you know, like it's like obviously the silver surfer is going to win that battle.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:35.940
So he has, yeah, he has the superhero, the superhuman strength.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:40.380
He has probably, I don't know, he's probably like invulnerable to a bunch of things.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:47.660
You know, it's like Superman scale where it kind of becomes boring, but it's interesting because he doesn't deal with Earth on a daily basis.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.820
He deals with like larger, like galactic problems.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.380
Magic, magic realms.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.160
Actually, that part gets weird.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:05.220
And I know that you're referencing the game there, but like we're going to have to unpack that towards the end because it's a bit of a spoiler for the end.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:11.720
So we'll save it. But I actually think he deals with that stuff a lot less, which is weird that it became the game setting.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:17.640
The game is, was made by Software Creations, published by Arcadia Systems.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:31.620
And it is a shmup, which is interesting because I guess like I've now been trained by most of the shmups that we've played on the NES to be vehicles and not people.

00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:36.280
Like I'm not saying you have to be in space to be a shmup, but you generally are a vehicle.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:42.380
And to just say like the silver surfer as a shmup, like couldn't like you just you could make any superhero a shmup game, right?

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:44.540
Like Spider-Man's a shmup and he just shoots webs.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:48.040
Captain America is a shmup and he just throws his shield.

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.400
Yeah, but it's I feel like it does.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:54.660
I mean, I guess if they're just walking like in gun smoke or gun dot smoke, as we called it.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:09:01.060
But like, I feel like, you know, Spider-Man is tough because you have to be you have to sort of be auto scrolling.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.180
Well, we kind of just did that with with Punisher.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:14.680
And I think this still could fit your definition, Mike, of of a shmup, because who's to say you're controlling Silver Surfer?

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:23.860
It's it looks like you're controlling his surfboard and he just happens to be riding you unless, you know, I don't know the lore.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:30.100
Maybe maybe he and his surfboard are one in the same, but I'll let you get into that.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.640
No, they're not the same.

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:37.740
That would be funny, though, if like that was a plot thing of like we just have to steal his surfboard and then he's powerless.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.700
Would you you would consider Punisher a shmup?

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:51.780
I think like it was auto scrolling and you probably you had basically the same amount of control over your character as you would in a shmup.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:54.180
It just happened to be like in a different axis.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.840
Yeah, I guess I guess I that's true.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:00.580
Something about the perspective, like what would you consider like time crisis?

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:02.760
What is that? I was calling it a shooter rail shooter.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.220
And it probably is more of that.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:13.700
But if we're going to start to get like existential on what a shmup is, then I feel like you could you could make the argument at the very least.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.920
Right. Well, there's definitely no denying that Silver Surfer is a shmup.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:28.620
And I guess I'm just saying that that's a rather boring choice for a superhero game to be a shmup because it's just kind of like fire a bunch of projectiles at enemies as the stage auto scrolls.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:33.080
And I feel like half the fun of being the superhero is flexing off your powers.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:46.260
Right. This game doesn't give you the opportunity to do much, much cool things other than just fire off these projectiles of which I would say like, you know, Silver Surfer does have the ability to manipulate energy and stuff.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:51.980
So sure, he could be doing this in the comics, but he doesn't like his primary means of attack is like firing off beams.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:11:08.680
I guess that's why I had to ask, because, you know, what you really do in this game is be on a surfboard and shoot what could just be a generic projectile that like you could put like Elmo as the guy on the surfboard and it would still make sense.

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:09.820
You know what I mean? I don't know.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.780
I don't know why I brought Elmo in this.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:14.280
You're just always trying to bring Elmo into things.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:16.540
And Elmo don't like that.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:22.960
I'm sure. This game also, as a shmup, doesn't doesn't stick to one point of view.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:26.120
It does both side scrolling and overhead stages alternating.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:34.700
So the game is mostly known, at least on the YouTube side of things, for being an incredibly difficult game.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:41.920
But I feel like that is mostly because of the angry video game nerd, which is I don't know who needs to hear this.

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:51.040
Not a historical account of video games, but a entertainment production put on for you, the viewer, to enjoy the content that you're watching.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:56.160
I wouldn't say that like when I was playing Silver Surfer, I thought it was the most difficult game we played.

00:11:56.300 --> 00:12:01.360
Sure, it's very difficult, but it's not like it's not frustratingly broken by any means.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:07.380
There's definitely some design choices that make it feel like that, though.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:10.900
Well, the hitbox. The hitbox is absolutely one of them.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:27.840
The other two being just the amount of sponginess to some of the enemies, especially when you first start off and you don't really have any power-up stuff going.

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:34.360
That if we were playing Gradius or something, they would all be like one-hit kills.

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.280
It's not so much.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.900
And then the...

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:45.680
I think it's just like some of the stages, it's kind of unclear what isn't is not a...

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.580
Something you can sort of travel over.

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:49.460
I mean, it's got to be the biggest offender.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:53.600
That was very prominent for me.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:56.100
Oftentimes, it looked like I could...

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:58.180
Something was in the background, it turns out to be in the foreground.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:03.480
And then something I'm avoiding for several tries, and then I realize, wait a minute, this isn't even here.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.040
It just looks like it's here.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:06.400
Yeah, right.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.300
I also had...

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:14.340
Sometimes had issues with enemies just kind of spawning at times that I couldn't have possibly...

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:18.800
Or at least it feels like I couldn't have possibly reacted to it until I had died once and known it was coming.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:21.680
So that was kind of frustrating.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:25.460
Well, I think that comes down to a huge problem with this game being a shmup.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:31.980
Is like, Sean, you said it well that in Gradius or most shmups, everything else is also...

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:36.720
Like, you're a one-hit KO, but so is mostly everything else aside from large enemies.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.960
When you blast them, they go off the screen.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:43.120
That is very untrue in this game, especially at the beginning.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.180
The surfer feels weak.

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:49.000
It takes a long time to get any additional orbs.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.460
You know, they're so worth it, and they change the gameplay dramatically.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.780
But it takes a long time to collect them.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:14:00.760
And your overall, like, power ability is collected via these letters that you pick up.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:04.740
F, B, S, and the orbs.

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:07.780
But all those things aren't, like, given out, like, candy.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:11.100
So for a long time in this game, it is really...

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.760
It's really tough because of how weak the surfer is comparatively.

00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:23.880
And I think that's just such a strange choice to make a cosmic being weak to, like, some enemies that, like, I swear...

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.880
I don't know where they pull these enemies out of because you'll have, like...

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.740
You'll have, like, cool space stuff.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.320
Then you'll have, like, ghosts.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:35.060
Ghosts. And then you'll just have, like, two 17th century cannons.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.560
Like, it's like, what are these doing in space?

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:39.040
Don't forget about the dinosaurs.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:45.680
Yes. But the cannons specifically, like, made me question, like, where these sprites came from.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:50.040
Like, were they all aware that they were designing a game under the same, like, setting?

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:53.760
Or were they like, okay, you're going to design these sprites, you're going to design these sprites.

00:14:53.880 --> 00:14:55.500
And then they all wind up in the same game.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.680
Yeah. Was this, like, intended to be a silver surfer game?

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:01.400
Or did they just, like, kind of plop them into this other game?

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:03.080
It doesn't feel like...

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.560
Because, okay, so the ghost stuff, right?

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:08.120
Like, that happens in Mephisto's world.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:14.120
And Mephisto's kind of like a Satan-like character in the Marvel Universe.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.420
So why isn't his level, like, more healthy?

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:21.560
Like, I get the ghost a little bit, but they're, like, popping out of doors.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.060
And they're supposed to be, like...

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.640
I don't know. It's kind of silly.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:27.940
The cannons, though, don't make any sense in Mephisto's world.

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:30.040
But the dinosaurs kind of do make sense.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.200
Because then you're taking on...

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.360
Forgive me, I don't know his name.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:34.280
But you're taking on that dinosaur guy.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.640
And that's like, okay, cool.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.640
I get it. Like, he's a reptile.

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.420
He is a...

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:42.640
Isn't Reptile also in, like, Mortal Kombat?

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:46.920
Just a character. Like, that's kind of funny that there's, like, a character that can just get away with being called Reptile.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.400
I think this one has a Y instead of an I.

00:15:49.640 --> 00:15:50.640
Oh, that is so cool.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.200
That's so rad. Yeah.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.420
